SUMMARY:MACRO Seminar: Fahad Sale h\, University of Florida - The Economi
 cs of Regulating Tokenized Securities
LOCATION:North Hall 2111
DESCRIPTION:Speaker: Fahad Sale h\, University of Florida\nTitle: "The Ec
 onomics of Regulating Tokenized Securities"\nHosted by: Rod Garratt\n\nW
 e develop an economic model to study the effect of regulation on tokeniz
 ed securities markets. Tokenizing a security does not exempt it from sec
 urities laws\, so in our framework token issuers must choose a complianc
 e policy that restricts trading. We characterize the resulting trade-off
  between regulatory stringency and financial market outcomes\, and we de
 rive three main results. First\, tighter regulation reduces the liquidit
 y of the tokenized market. Second\, tokenization is not commercially via
 ble for sufficiently strict regulation. Third\, the tightest level of re
 gulation that tokenization can withstand depends on the characteristics 
 of the tokenized asset.\n\nhttps://econ.ucsb.edu/events/all/2026/macro-s
 eminar-fahad-saleh-university-florida
URL:https://econ.ucsb.edu/events/all/2026/macro-seminar-fahad-saleh-unive
 rsity-florida
CATEGORIES:MACRO
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
