SUMMARY:MACRO Seminar: Yang Gao\, University of Auckland
LOCATION:North Hall 2111
DESCRIPTION:Speaker: Yang Gao\, University of Auckland\nHosted by: Yueyua
 n Ma\n\nYang Gao is a lecturer in the Department of Economics at the Uni
 versity of Auckland Business School\, New Zealand. She holds a Ph.D. in 
 Economics from the University of California\, Santa Barbara. Her researc
 h interests lie in macroeconomics\, environmental economics\, and energy
  economics\, with related interests in firm dynamics and finance. Her cu
 rrent work studies the macroeconomic and welfare implications of climate
  change and climate and energy policies\, with a particular focus on how
  market frictions shape policy outcomes. Her work combines quantitative 
 macroeconomic modeling with econometric analyses of micro- and macro-lev
 el data and theoretical analysis.\n\nhttps://econ.ucsb.edu/events/all/20
 27/macro-seminar-yang-gao-university-auckland
URL:https://econ.ucsb.edu/events/all/2027/macro-seminar-yang-gao-universi
 ty-auckland
